# `#[patch]`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

PATCH shorthand for `#[route(PATCH, path, ...)]` inside an HTTP `#[handlers]` implementation.

```rust
#[patch("/{id}")]
async fn patch(&self, Path(id): Path<u64>, Json(input): Json<UserPatch>) -> Json<User> { todo!() }
```

It accepts an optional controller-relative string path followed by the shared route modifiers. `#[patch]` and `#[patch(streamed)]` mount at the controller base. It is a consumed marker, not a standalone function attribute. See [`#[route]`](./route) for complete grammar, modifier rules, containment, generated artifacts, and feature behavior.
